    "proved_in_stated_scope": [
      "BO: for the same fixed smooth unforced viscosity-one periodic NS solution, an additional positive terminal energy atom of mass m defines last-threshold times t_r with q_r(t_r)=m/2 and q_r(t)>m/2 for every later t<T. Ordered radius/time quantifiers and radial monotonicity are retained.",
      "Writing delta_r=T-t_r and global D_r=integral from t_r to T of ||grad u||_2^2, D_r tends to zero and D_r>=c m delta_r/r^2. This is not a localized weighted-dissipation lower bound.",
      "The complete signed local energy balance gives N_r>=m/8+D_chi,r for small r; all transport and pressure terms are retained in fixed zero-mean pressure gauge.",
      "Periodic Calderon-Zygmund and known Gagliardo-Nirenberg/time Holder estimates give delta_r D_r^3>=c m^4 E^(-3)r^4. Consequently r^4=o(delta_r), delta_r=o(r^2), and D_r>=c m^(5/4)E^(-3/4)r^(1/2).",
      "The derived necessary inequalities have not produced a contradiction with finite total dissipation. BO.18 checks only the algebraic compatibility of powers delta~r^(5/2),D~r^(1/2), not realization by NS."
    ],
    "limitations": [
      "No terminal atom existence or exclusion, general regularity, arbitrary-singularity BL.3 generation, G or original-input reduction is established.",
